    "goal": "Co-incubate CYP2D6 with testosterone in the presence of a competitive inhibitor and characterize the inhibition kinetics.",
    "rationale": "CYP2D6 is incubated with testosterone as substrate at 1991.1 µM (Km = 911.2 µM, so [S] ≈ 2.2× Km, near-saturating). A competitive inhibitor (Ki = 130.5 µM) is present at 83.2 µM. Vmax = 9.985 µmol/min. The [I]/[S] molar ratio is ~0.042, and [I]/Ki ≈ 0.64, so competitive inhibition is expected to reduce the reaction rate substantially. All concentrations are in µM and Vmax in µmol/min.",
